# A condition and a print at a stop in an image `jet build` made may use an
# operation the program never runs: the program only adds and takes
# remainders, so its image holds none of the runtime's code for a product
# or an ordering of Ints that outgrow a word. The evaluation's own code does
# both and calls the runtime only for such Ints, so a value that fits a word
# evaluates, and one that doesn't stops at a trap that names the runtime
# function the image lacks. Before, setting the condition or printing
# refused each such expression, whatever its value. step's x is 4, 11,
# then 26; the condition first holds at 11.
# The fixture must stay in jet fmt form: line 3 is step's last line and
# line 7 run's first.
fixture: NewOperationsAtAStop.fixture
env: NO_COLOR=1
env: PATH={work}/no-tools
step: jet build -O0 prog.jet
exit: 0
step: jet debug {work}/.jet/build/prog --break prog.jet:7
stdin: new_operations_at_a_stop_evaluate.stdin
exit: 0
stdout: ~ "Breakpoint set  prog.jet:3 if x * 2 > 20\nThe condition runs in the program: a hit where it is false runs on without a stop\n" # the condition runs in the program
stdout: ~ "Breakpoint hit  prog.jet:3  in step()\n3 |     (y + x) % 1000        <- here\nLocals:  x = 11   y = 14\n" # and stops where it first holds
stdout: ~ "print x * 3\nx * 3 = 33\n" # a product the program never takes
stdout: ~ "print y * y > x\ny * y > x = true\n" # an ordering it never takes
stdout: ~ "Can't evaluate `x * 1000000000000000000`: it needs the runtime's `jet_int_mul`, which the running image does not hold: the program never needed it\n" # a product past a word names what the image lacks
stdout: ~ "\n57\n" # the program runs to its total
stdout: ~ "Program finished\n" # and its end
